# !! EVIDENCE RETRACTED 2026-08-17 !!
# The KameOS-vs-SOVIET comparison below was made against KameOS's EMBEDDED
# config -- which is a decoy. Those trees redirect config_data.gz at a
# checked-in stock defconfig (KameOS serves Xiaomi's 4.14.180 stock config from
# a 4.14.356 kernel), so "KameOS has DT_OVERLAY off" describes Xiaomi's 2020
# config, NOT what Zundamon compiled. The reasoning below is unsupported.
# Kept only because stock raphael genuinely did use a self-contained appended
# DTB, so the setting is still worth one empirical test -- as a guess, not a
# deduction. See scripts/verify_kernel_config.py for the decoy detector.
#
# Make a SOVIET/openela-tree kernel bootable on KameOS v3.303 (HyperOS 3).
#
# Five Docker-capable kernels from three trees all fail to boot on KameOS while
# a control (KameOS's own kernel, same repack) boots -- and the device POWERS
# OFF rather than bootlooping, which points at device-tree/regulator init long
# before userspace.
#
# Diffing KameOS's embedded config against the SOVIET build narrowed the
# DTB-relevant delta to exactly one symbol. Both trees set
# BUILD_ARM64_APPENDED_DTB_IMAGE=y and both use the same
# BUILD_ARM64_APPENDED_KERNEL_IMAGE_NAME="Image.gz-dtb" with an empty
# ..._DTB_IMAGE_NAMES, so the appended-DTB machinery is not the difference:
#
#   CONFIG_BUILD_ARM64_DT_OVERLAY   SOVIET=y   KameOS=n
#
# With DT_OVERLAY on, the appended device tree is a *base* that expects the
# bootloader to apply overlays from the dtbo partition. KameOS flashed its own
# dtbo, built for its own base DTB, so a SOVIET kernel lands with overlays that
# do not match its tree -- consistent with the early power-off. Turning it off
# makes the appended DTB self-contained, the way KameOS's kernel ships it.
#
# Deliberately NOT copied from KameOS's config:
#   CONFIG_ARM64_LSE_ATOMICS -- KameOS has it off, SOVIET on. Forcing it off on
#   this tree breaks the build: arch/arm64/include/asm/cmpxchg.h:51-59
#   "error: expected string literal in 'asm'". It has no bearing on boot, so
#   the tree's own value stays.
#
# This is a hypothesis under test, not a proven fix. Verify with
# `fastboot boot` (RAM only) before flashing anything -- and remember a failure
# powers raphael off, so it needs a physical power press to come back.
# CONFIG_BUILD_ARM64_DT_OVERLAY is not set
CONFIG_BUILD_ARM64_APPENDED_DTB_IMAGE=y
CONFIG_BUILD_ARM64_APPENDED_KERNEL_IMAGE_NAME="Image.gz-dtb"
